 "brief": "A hand crank lever in PA12 (SLS). It is 10 mm thick (z = 0 to 10) and fits on an 8 mm shaft along Z at x = 0, y = 0 (a tight fit, glued, so the shaft holds it completely). At x = 80 a knob screws in with an M5 thread, 10 mm deep, from the top face (z = 10); the hand holds the knob 20 mm above that face. Keep the lever inside x = -12 to 92, y = -12 to 12. Cranking is 70 N on the knob across the lever (Y), a hundred thousand times over its life; leaning on it is 50 N downward (-Z). It should not flex more than 1 mm at the knob. Safety factor 2.5.",
